Here's the complete process from **zero to running a Maven project**.

# Step 1: Install Java

Download and install JDK 17 (or newer):

[Oracle JDK Downloads](https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/downloads/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Verify installation:

```bash
java -version
javac -version
```

---

# Step 2: Install Maven

Download Maven:

[Apache Maven Download](https://maven.apache.org/download.cgi?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Verify installation:

```bash
mvn -version
```

You should see output similar to:

```text
Apache Maven 3.x.x
Java version: 17
```

---

# Step 3: Install IntelliJ IDEA (Easiest Option)

Download:

[IntelliJ IDEA Community Edition](https://www.jetbrains.com/idea/download/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Install and open it.

---

# Step 4: Create a Maven Project

In IntelliJ:

```text
File
  → New Project
      → Maven
          → Next
```

Enter:

```text
GroupId: com.example
ArtifactId: demo
```

Click **Create**.

IntelliJ creates:

```text
demo
 ├─ pom.xml
 ├─ src
 │   ├─ main
 │   │   └─ java
 │   └─ test
 │       └─ java
```

---

# Step 5: Open pom.xml

You will see a file named:

```text
pom.xml
```

Put this code inside:

```xml
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>
    <version>1.0</version>

    <properties>
        <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>
        <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>
    </properties>
</project>
```

---

# Step 6: Create Java Class

Inside:

```text
src/main/java
```

Create:

```java
package com.example;

public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello Maven");
    }
}
```

---

# Step 7: Open Maven Window

In IntelliJ:

```text
View
  → Tool Windows
      → Maven
```

You will see:

```text
Lifecycle
 ├─ clean
 ├─ validate
 ├─ compile
 ├─ test
 ├─ package
 ├─ install
 └─ deploy
```

This is the Maven lifecycle.

---

# Step 8: Run Compile Phase

Double-click:

```text
compile
```

or run:

```bash
mvn compile
```

Result:

```text
Java code compiled
```

---

# Step 9: Run Test Phase

Double-click:

```text
test
```

or:

```bash
mvn test
```

Result:

```text
Tests executed
```

---

# Step 10: Run Package Phase

Double-click:

```text
package
```

or:

```bash
mvn package
```

Maven automatically runs:

```text
validate
↓
compile
↓
test
↓
package
```

A JAR file is created in:

```text
target/demo-1.0.jar
```

---

# Step 11: Run Install Phase

Double-click:

```text
install
```

or:

```bash
mvn install
```

Maven runs:

```text
validate
↓
compile
↓
test
↓
package
↓
install
```

The JAR is copied to:

```text
.m2/repository
```

(local Maven repository)

---

# Step 12: Clean Project

Run:

```bash
mvn clean
```

or double-click:

```text
clean
```

This deletes:

```text
target/
```

---

# Interview Answer (Short)

**Maven lifecycle phases:**

```text
validate
→ compile
→ test
→ package
→ install
→ deploy
```

**Commands:**

```bash
mvn clean
mvn compile
mvn test
mvn package
mvn install
mvn deploy
```

**Tool used:**

* Java JDK
* Apache Maven
* IntelliJ IDEA (recommended) or Visual Studio Code

For learning Maven, the easiest path is:

**Install JDK → Install Maven → Install IntelliJ → Create Maven Project → Edit `pom.xml` → Run Compile → Package → Install.**
